{"kind":"assert","text":"J4: please do not edit the private binding. Ruling dcf500c5 builder decision 2 asked whether the later chain compares the binding to V15's digest. It does, so the planned edit would refuse every later admission and phase. V13 is stopped before freeze and needs your ruling on the three options below. I recommend A.\n\nThe comparison, which I read at source:\n- Later recovery.mjs:170 and :172 call collect. :158 has collect call setupClosure. :144 has setupClosure run the V15 packet's own old.loadAdmission, and :34 and :142 pin that module to 7fef0a8b. V11's recovery.mjs has that digest.\n- V11 recovery.mjs:186 reads the private binding's current bytes. :191 puts its path, size and digest in the record it rebuilds. :222 stops with setup-admission-predecessor-changed if that record differs from the V15 admission.\n\nWhat it does live, by that reading: the later admission writer refuses before it creates a namespace. A binding edited after the later admission refuses at each phase. Restoring the old bytes after admission does not help, because each phase rereads the file.\n\nObserved by the agent in a rehearsal copy, with a rehearsal binding and the stand-in provider; I read the Source and did not rerun these. With the binding null at setup and the path written before the later admission, the writer ended admission-unavailable, and a stderr print added in a second run showed setup-admission-predecessor-changed as the word beneath it. With no edit, the admission gave later-admission-created, and work then halted noncanonical-path, because the field is null. So leaving the binding null with V12's code also fails, before work's first original. Earlier rehearsals missed this because the harness wrote the path into the binding before setup (rehearse-later.mjs:228).\n\nOptions:\n\nA, recommended. Leave the private binding unchanged, with the field null. operator.mjs:308 reads the fixed path \u003cvault\u003e/mint-read/independent-read.json, the path you named, instead of the binding's field. V15's digest stays valid. The change is one line plus a rehearsal correction, and a wrong value can no longer reach this read. It reverses \"I will set it\" in your decision 2. You still put the file at that path after rehold. The operator keeps checking the file's contract and provenance.\n\nB. You create a second private file for the later packet, holding the old values plus the path, and V13's FIXED.privateBinding names it. The V15 path stays unchanged for the V15 check. This keeps your value in a binding, adds one custody file and adds one more thing to review.\n\nC, not recommended. Replace the call at :144 with a new check that skips the private binding. This is the largest change, and it drops the re-read of the V15 admission.\n\nState of V13: nothing is frozen, and no index, qualification or controls exist. The code for the checker's items 1, 2, 3 and 5 is applied and not yet passing: one scenario matched, and clean and leftovers-at-push-a reach their expected words and fail their new row checks. Your 404 ruling, the release text, the names and the checker's item 4 are not started. The rest does not depend on which option you pick, so the agent can continue on them while you rule, and it freezes only after your ruling.\n\nNo private path was read or changed, and nothing live ran.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dcf500c5262bd4c0969186fab8ad435228081467 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 19 more"}}